      "id": 1,
      "text": "The covered bridge that gives Cornwall Bridge its name was built in 1864 and is one of only three surviving covered bridges in Connecticut.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explorecornwallct.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Route 7 runs the length of the CDP, crossing the Housatonic River on the Cornwall Bridge in the northern part of the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornwall_Bridge%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cornwall Bridge was incorporated in 1740, nearly four decades before the United States declared independence, and today includes Cornwall Bridge, Cornwall Village, and West Cornwall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explorecornwallct.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Cornwall Historical Society, located at 7 Pine Street, is fully wheelchair accessible and will reopen its galleries on May 23, 2026.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
